.TH PIPEDUCK 1 "October 2026" "pipeduck 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pipeduck \- automatic audio ducking for PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pipeduck
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pipeduck
lowers music, games, videos and other playback while speech is detected in a
selected voice-call stream, in the local microphone, or both. It is designed for
PipeWire desktops and is normally controlled from a StatusNotifierItem tray icon.
.PP
Audio is routed through a temporary virtual sink. The virtual sink monitor volume
is faded down and smoothly back to 100% with a configurable smoothstep ramp.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tray
Start the tray (default).
.TP
.B status
Show the default sink, playback streams, trigger and current tuning.
.TP
.B sources
List playback streams selectable as call audio.
.TP
.BI "select-source " ID
Save a playback stream as the voice-call source.
.TP
.B mic-sources
List microphones selectable for microphone-triggered ducking.
.TP
.BI "select-mic " "NAME|ID"
Save a microphone by source name or index.
.TP
.B tune
Open the terminal tuner.
.TP
.B tune-gui
Open the GTK4 tuner when built with GUI support.
.TP
.B route
Route streams and duck until interrupted. Requires
.BR \-\-yes\-really\-route .
.TP
.B route-once
Route for a few seconds as a diagnostic. Requires
.BR \-\-yes\-really\-route .
.TP
.B config-path
Print the configuration file path.
.TP
.B init-config
Create a default configuration if none exists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-duck\-percent " N
Volume for non-call audio while speech is active (0-100).
.TP
.BI "\-\-vad\-threshold " F
Base RMS threshold for call audio. Speech starts above about twice this value.
.TP
.BI "\-\-mic\-vad\-threshold " F
Base RMS threshold for microphone-triggered ducking. Defaults to the value of
\fB\-\-vad\-threshold\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-\-hold\-ms " N
Keep ducking active for N milliseconds after speech stops.
.TP
.BI "\-\-fade\-ms " N
Smooth return time in milliseconds (overrides release_fade_ms).
.TP
.BI "\-\-trigger " MODE
One of
.IR call ,
.I mic
or
.IR both .
.TP
.BI "\-\-seconds " N
Duration for route-once (default 5).
.TP
.B \-\-yes\-really\-route
Acknowledge that the command changes the live PipeWire graph.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pipeduck/config.toml
Configuration file. Changes are polled by a running tray and applied live.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the base configuration directory.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used for the single-instance tray lock.
.TP
.B PIPEDUCK_ICON_THEME_PATH
Overrides the icon theme search path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error. Diagnostic routing commands also return 1 when the
safety flag is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR pw-link (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR wireplumber (1)
